            <ArticleTitle>Elevated amylase levels as a result of self-induced hypersalivation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>585-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with recurrent vomiting, abdominal pain, and elevated serum amylase activity may have pancreatitis. Although elevated serum amylase levels are a sensitive indicator for acute pancreatitis, this test is not highly specific for pancreatic disease. A patient is described who illustrates the need for specific laboratory, historical, and occasional psychological evaluation in pediatric patients with elevated amylase values.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
